course: dictionary
lesson: 2039
title: Congo: a river, a forest, two countries
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Congo starts with a capital letter because it is a proper noun, the name of one particular place. Words like Congo do not work like ordinary words, so you cannot just swap in a meaning. «The Congo is the deepest river known» tells you Congo is the name of a river.
explain: Congo is used for more than one thing. «The okapi lives only in the Congo forest» means the rainforest, while the Republic of the Congo and the Democratic Republic of the Congo are countries. The words around the name are the clues: river, forest, country or capital tell you which Congo is meant.
explain: If the clues are missing, check an atlas or a dictionary. Pupils often learn about the Congo in geography, where they find the river and the rainforest on a map. A map or a dictionary is the right tool for names, while context helps with ordinary words.
fact: Congo is a proper noun, so it always starts with a capital letter.
fact: The Congo is a great river in central Africa, and it is the second-longest river in Africa.
fact: The Congo is the deepest river in the world; «the Congo River has more than seven hundred kinds of fish».
fact: Congo is also part of the names of two countries: the Democratic Republic of the Congo (capital Kinshasa) and the Republic of the Congo (capital Brazzaville).
fact: The Congo Basin rainforest is the second-largest rainforest on Earth, after the Amazon.
exercise: «The Congo is the deepest river known.» What kind of word is Congo here? | A plural noun, more than one thing | An adjective, a describing word | *A proper noun, the name of a river | A verb, a doing word
exercise: «The okapi lives only in the Congo forest.» Which Congo is the forest in? | *The Congo Basin, a great rainforest | The Sahara, a hot desert | The Amazon in South America | The Himalayas, mountains in Asia
exercise: Which capital city belongs to the Democratic Republic of the Congo? | Nairobi | Lagos | *Kinshasa | Brazzaville
test: Which rainforest is the second-largest on Earth, after the Amazon? | The Black Forest in Germany | *The Congo Basin | The Daintree in Australia | The Sahara
test: What is the capital city of the Republic of the Congo? | *Brazzaville | Kinshasa | Lagos | Nairobi
exam: Which statement about the Congo is true? | The Congo is a small town in Europe | *The Congo is the second-longest river in Africa | The Congo is a desert with no water | The Congo is in South America, beside the Amazon
